# core/resolve-element - Which IRI does this name refer to?
#
# Answers: candidate resources whose label, alternative label or native
# identifier matches TERM, with their types and the graph they came from, best
# candidate first.
#
# Does NOT prove: that the best-ranked match is the one the user meant. Two
# applications may share a label across two models. When more than one candidate
# comes back and the choice changes the answer, ask rather than pick.
#
# Run this before any template taking an IRI. Never construct an IRI from a
# label: the minted form is {base}{notation}/{modelId}/element/{localId}, and the
# local id is the source tool's, so guessing it is guessing twice.
#
# Matching is case-insensitive and substring, across the label roles and the
# native id. Two columns say how good a hit is, and both are ordered on:
#
#   ?rank     "1 exact", "2 prefix", "3 contains" - how much of the value matched
#   ?matched  "1 name", "2 alias", "3 id"         - what kind of thing matched
#
# Both are numbered strings so a plain ORDER BY puts the best candidate first with
# no scoring arithmetic anyone has to trust. Carried from core/resolve-model,
# which needed the same thing for the same reason.
#
# The numbering is not cosmetic. This template ORDERED BY the role name alone, and
# unnumbered names sort alphabetically: altLabel, nativeId, prefLabel. So a name
# match sorted BELOW an id match, and LIMIT discarded names first. Measured on
# fixtures/base.trig: TERM="e" at the default LIMIT 25 returned 23 native-id hits,
# 2 alias hits and NOT ONE of the 63 name matches available. A match on a native id
# ("APP-1") means something different from a match on a name, and a caller resolving
# a phrase a human typed wants the names.
#
# Parameters: TERM, LIMIT
{{PREFIXES}}
SELECT ?rank ?matched ?value ?element ?type ?g
WHERE {
  {{GRAPH_OPEN:semantic}}
    {
      ?element {{ROLE:label}} ?value .
      BIND("1 name" AS ?matched)
    }
    UNION
    {
      ?element {{ROLE:alt_label}} ?value .
      BIND("2 alias" AS ?matched)
    }
    UNION
    {
      ?element {{PATH:native_id}} ?value .
      BIND("3 id" AS ?matched)
    }
    FILTER(CONTAINS(LCASE(STR(?value)), LCASE({{TERM}})))
    BIND(
      IF(LCASE(STR(?value)) = LCASE({{TERM}}), "1 exact",
        IF(STRSTARTS(LCASE(STR(?value)), LCASE({{TERM}})), "2 prefix", "3 contains")
      ) AS ?rank
    )
    OPTIONAL {
      ?element a ?type .
      FILTER(?type != {{ROLE:concept_class}} && ?type != {{ROLE:element_class}})
    }
  {{GRAPH_CLOSE}}
}
ORDER BY ?rank ?matched ?value ?element
LIMIT {{LIMIT}}
